message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Location, location, location: TabPFN-3.5 vs spatial models on São Paulo ITBI transactions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Benvenho"
    given-names: "Agnaldo Calvi"
    orcid: ""
    affiliation: "BP Avaliações e Perícias / IBAPE Nacional"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - mass appraisal
  - real estate valuation
  - TabPFN
  - tabular foundation models
  - spatial cross-validation
  - ITBI
  - "São Paulo"
abstract: >-
  Does a tabular foundation model need spatial features? TabPFN-3.5 with the
  plain table (coordinates as two numeric columns, no spatial modelling) is
  compared with OLS, a SAR lag model and XGBoost with spatial features on
  82,187 declared transaction prices from the São Paulo real-estate transfer
  tax (ITBI), under spatial-block cross-validation and an out-of-time test
  on 47,810 transactions of 2026, with pre-registered refutation criteria
  including residual Moran's I. Includes a Streamlit app and permutation
  SHAP. Prior Labs TabPFN-3.5 Hackathon entry.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
